  "lesson5Card5Title": "Parameters",
  "lesson5Card5Speech": "A function can get a value when you call it. The value goes into a parameter. A parameter is like a variable box from Lesson 1. Each call puts a new value in the box.",
  "lesson5Card5Tip": "The parameter goes inside the `()` of `def`.",
  "lesson5Card6Title": "return: give a value back",
  "lesson5Card6Speech": "A function can give a value back. Use `return`. Here, `add` adds two numbers. It gives the answer back. We keep it in a variable.",
  "lesson5Card6Tip": "`return` sends the answer back to where you called the function.",
